# UI Design Rules — Lectur.io

## Design Direction
**"Premium EdTech" aesthetic** — Light gray base, sophisticated, and focused.
Think: Linear.app × Vercel Dashboard. Clean geometry, purposeful motion, high information density without clutter.

---

## Color System

```css
:root {
  /* Backgrounds — layered depth */
  --bg-base:    #f4f4f5;   /* page background (zinc-100) */
  --bg-surface: #ffffff;   /* cards, panels */
  --bg-overlay: #e4e4e7;   /* hover states, modals */
  --bg-border:  #d4d4d8;   /* subtle borders */

  /* Text */
  --text-primary:   #18181b;
  --text-secondary: #52525b;
  --text-muted:     #71717a;

  /* Accent — one color only */
  --accent:         #6366f1;   /* indigo — learning / focus */
  --accent-hover:   #4f46e5;
  --accent-subtle:  rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.15);

  /* Semantic */
  --success: #22c55e;
  --warning: #f59e0b;
  --error:   #ef4444;
}
```

**Rules:**
- Light gray background as default — use `--bg-base` and layered surfaces
- Accent color (`--accent`) used sparingly: primary CTA, active states, progress indicators
- Never use multiple accent colors — one is enough
- Gradients only for hero/marketing sections, not functional UI

---

## Typography

```css
/* Font stack */
font-family: "Geist", "Inter Tight", -apple-system, sans-serif;

/* Scale */
--text-xs:   0.75rem;   /* 12px — labels, captions */
--text-sm:   0.875rem;  /* 14px — secondary content */
--text-base: 1rem;      /* 16px — body */
--text-lg:   1.125rem;  /* 18px — card titles */
--text-xl:   1.25rem;   /* 20px — section headers */
--text-2xl:  1.5rem;    /* 24px — page titles */
--text-3xl:  1.875rem;  /* 30px — hero subheadings */
--text-4xl:  2.25rem;   /* 36px — hero headlines */

/* Letter spacing */
--tracking-tight:  -0.03em;  /* headlines */
--tracking-normal: -0.01em;  /* body */
--tracking-wide:   0.08em;   /* labels, badges */
```

**Rules:**
- Headlines: `font-weight: 600`, `letter-spacing: -0.03em`
- Body: `font-weight: 400`, `line-height: 1.7`
- Labels/badges: `text-transform: uppercase`, `letter-spacing: 0.08em`, `font-size: 11px`
- Never use `font-weight: 700` or bold — 600 semibold is the max

